@prefix : <http://example.org/orexis/world/layby#> .
@prefix courier: <http://example.org/orexis/courier#> .
@prefix orexis: <http://example.org/orexis#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

<> a orexis:BeliefGraph .    # this document is one graph, and this is what it is
<> orexis:ownedBy :courier_a .    # and whose it is — said here, never by the file's name

#  WHAT THE COURIER BELIEVES AS THE WORLD IS POSED — its parcel, where the parcel and its driver stand, and
#  not where any van is. Where a van is comes from outside, by a fix or a contact, and what comes from outside
#  is stored when it arrives and never asserted: the first fix says van A's cell and the courier's transitions
#  keep it current, so the agent plans nothing until its fix has reported; and van B's cell is its receiver's
#  to say, once within range. Of van B's driver it believes nothing: the van is driven by a driver it does not
#  play, which is all the drive's precondition asks.
:parcel_a a courier:Parcel ; courier:destination :east_end ; rdfs:label "the parcel owed at the eastern end" .
:parcel_a courier:x 1 ; courier:y 1 .
:east_end courier:x 6 ; courier:y 1 ; rdfs:label "the eastern end of the lane, where parcel A is owed" .
:driver_a courier:aboard :van_a .
